{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/yin/repl/ast_query_e2e_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.ast-query-e2e-test\n     2\t  \"End-to-end acceptance tests for the REPL AST indexer and query bridge\n     3\t   ($ast and $occ) across all four supported VM models (ast-walker, semantic,\n     4\t   stack, register).\"\n     5\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n     6\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     7\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n     8\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n     9\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    10\t            [yin.repl :as repl]\n    11\t            [yin.repl.ast-index :as ast-index]\n    12\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]))\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\t(def ^:private vm-types\n    16\t  (keys repl/vm-constructors))\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t(defn- evaluate\n    20\t  [state lines]\n    21\t  (reduce (fn [[state texts] line]\n    22\t            (let [[state' text] (repl/eval-input state line)]\n    23\t              [state' (conj texts text)]))\n    24\t          [state []]\n    25\t          lines))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn- q-line\n    29\t  \"A `dao.space.query/q` call on `query`, with `more` argument source\n    30\t   appended.\"\n    31\t  [query & more]\n    32\t  (str \"(dao.space.query/q (quote \" (pr-str query) \")\"\n    33\t       (apply str (map #(str \" \" %) more))\n    34\t       \")\"))\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(def ^:private require-line\n    38\t  \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\")\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn- stream-values\n    42\t  \"Every value currently on a stream, read from its oldest cursor.\"\n    43\t  [s]\n    44\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n    45\t         acc []]\n    46\t    (let [r (stream/next s cursor)]\n    47\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    48\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n    49\t        acc))))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- lossy-observer\n    53\t  \"An observer that reports a gap on its first read.\"\n    54\t  []\n    55\t  (let [writer (:dao.stream/handle\n    56\t                 (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    57\t                                ring/capacity-key 1}))\n    58\t        descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor (stream/descriptor writer))\n    59\t        lossy (observer/attach\n    60\t                (ring/make-attacher {(:dao.stream/identity descriptor)\n    61\t                                     writer})\n    62\t                descriptor)]\n    63\t    (doseq [v [1 2]]\n    64\t      (stream/append! writer (macro/ast->packet {:type :literal, :value v})))\n    65\t    lossy))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(def ^:private lost-warning\n    69\t  \"Warning: the AST index lost a program batch; $ast and $occ are unavailable until (reset)\")\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t;; =============================================================================\n    73\t;; 2. $ / $ast / $occ join via :yin/address\n    74\t;; =============================================================================\n    75\t\n    76\t(deftest join-dollar-ast-and-occ-via-yin-address\n    77\t  ;; Requirement 2: A $ / $ast / $occ join (e.g. a :yin/name from $ joined to\n    78\t  ;; the $ast row of the same node address via :yin/address).\n    79\t  (doseq [vm-type vm-types]\n    80\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n    81\t      (let [join-q '[:find ?name ?path\n    82\t                     :in $ $ast $occ ?name\n    83\t                     :where\n    84\t                     [?e :yin/name ?name]\n    85\t                     [?e :yin/address ?addr]\n    86\t                     [$ast ?addr :variable ?name]\n    87\t                     [$occ ?root ?path ?addr]]\n    88\t            [_ [_ _ res]]\n    89\t            (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n    90\t                      [require-line\n    91\t                       \"(defn inc [i] (+ i 1))\"\n    92\t                       (q-line join-q \"(quote i)\")])]\n    93\t        (is (= (pr-str '#{[i [[3 1] 3 [3 0]]]}) res)\n    94\t            \"the variable i in $ joins to $ast and $occ via its :yin/address\")))))\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t;; =============================================================================\n    98\t;; 3. Identical code under two different roots\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t\n   101\t(deftest identical-code-under-different-roots-shares-ast-rows-with-distinct-occurrences\n   102\t  ;; Requirement 3: Identical code evaluated under two different roots: shared\n   103\t  ;; $ast rows, distinct $occ occurrences.\n   104\t  (doseq [vm-type vm-types]\n   105\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n   106\t      (let [root-paths-q '[:find ?path\n   107\t                           :in $ast $occ ?op ?root\n   108\t                           :where\n   109\t                           [$ast ?node :variable ?op]\n   110\t                           [$occ ?root ?path ?node]]\n   111\t            occ-count-q '[:find (count ?path) .\n   112\t                          :with ?root\n   113\t                          :in $ast $occ ?op\n   114\t                          :where\n   115\t                          [$ast ?node :variable ?op]\n   116\t                          [$occ ?root ?path ?node]]\n   117\t            ast-count-q '[:find (count ?node) .\n   118\t                          :in $ast ?op\n   119\t                          :where\n   120\t                          [$ast ?node :variable ?op]]\n   121\t            [state _]\n   122\t            (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   123\t                      [require-line\n   124\t                       \"(+ 1 2)\"\n   125\t                       \"(* (+ 1 2) 3)\"])\n   126\t            packets (stream-values (:row-stream state))\n   127\t            inner-root (first (nth packets 1))\n   128\t            outer-root (first (nth packets 2))\n   129\t            [_ [inner-res outer-res occ-count ast-count]]\n   130\t            (evaluate state\n   131\t                      [(q-line root-paths-q \"(quote +)\"\n   132\t                               (str \"(quote \" (pr-str inner-root) \")\"))\n   133\t                       (q-line root-paths-q \"(quote +)\"\n   134\t                               (str \"(quote \" (pr-str outer-root) \")\"))\n   135\t                       (q-line occ-count-q \"(quote +)\")\n   136\t                       (q-line ast-count-q \"(quote +)\")])\n   137\t            rel (ast-index/relations (:ast-indexer state))\n   138\t            plus-nodes (set (keep (fn [[id tag n]]\n   139\t                                    (when (and (= :variable tag) (= '+ n)) id))\n   140\t                                  (:ast rel)))\n   141\t            plus-places (set (keep (fn [[r p n]]\n   142\t                                     (when (contains? plus-nodes n) [r p]))\n   143\t                                   (:occ rel)))]\n   144\t        (is (not= inner-root outer-root) \"two different programs have distinct roots\")\n   145\t        (is (= 1 (count plus-nodes))\n   146\t            \"the shared + node is one $ast row\")\n   147\t        (is (= \"1\" ast-count)\n   148\t            \"the shared + node appears exactly once in $ast\")\n   149\t        (is (= #{[inner-root [2]] [outer-root [[3 0] 2]]} plus-places)\n   150\t            \"$occ holds exactly the + node's place under each captured root\")\n   151\t        (is (= \"#{[[2]]}\" inner-res)\n   152\t            \"under the inner root, + sits only at [2]\")\n   153\t        (is (= \"#{[[[3 0] 2]]}\" outer-res)\n   154\t            \"under the outer root, + sits only at [[3 0] 2]\")\n   155\t        (is (= \"2\" occ-count)\n   156\t            \"the query sees exactly the two root-scoped places of +\")))))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t;; =============================================================================\n   160\t;; 4. Re-evaluating identical code\n   161\t;; =============================================================================\n   162\t\n   163\t(deftest re-evaluating-identical-code-adds-no-ast-rows-and-no-occ-tuples\n   164\t  ;; Requirement 4: Re-evaluating identical code adds no $ast rows and no $occ tuples.\n   165\t  (doseq [vm-type vm-types]\n   166\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n   167\t      (let [[s1 _] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   168\t                             [\"(+ 1 2)\"])\n   169\t            rel1 (ast-index/relations (:ast-indexer s1))\n   170\t            status1 (repl/repl-state s1)\n   171\t            [s2 texts2] (evaluate s1 [\"(+ 1 2)\"])\n   172\t            rel2 (ast-index/relations (:ast-indexer s2))\n   173\t            status2 (repl/repl-state s2)\n   174\t            [s3 texts3] (evaluate s2 [\"(+ 1 2)\"])\n   175\t            rel3 (ast-index/relations (:ast-indexer s3))\n   176\t            status3 (repl/repl-state s3)]\n   177\t        (is (= [\"3\"] texts2))\n   178\t        (is (= [\"3\"] texts3))\n   179\t        (is (= #{[:variable '+] [:literal 1] [:literal 2]}\n   180\t               (set (keep (fn [[_ tag v]]\n   181\t                            (when (#{:variable :literal} tag) [tag v]))\n   182\t                          (:ast rel1))))\n   183\t            \"the first evaluation populates $ast with the program's rows\")\n   184\t        (is (seq (:occ rel1))\n   185\t            \"the first evaluation populates $occ\")\n   186\t        (is (= (set (map first (:ast rel1)))\n   187\t               (set (map #(nth % 2) (:occ rel1))))\n   188\t            \"every $ast row has an occurrence, and every occurrence a row\")\n   189\t        (is (= 1 (count (set (map first (:occ rel1)))))\n   190\t            \"the first evaluation's occurrences sit under its one root\")\n   191\t        (is (= rel1 rel2 rel3)\n   192\t            \"repeated evaluation of identical code produces identical AST relations\")\n   193\t        (is (= (count (:ast rel1)) (count (:ast rel2)) (count (:ast rel3)))\n   194\t            \"no $ast rows are added\")\n   195\t        (is (= (count (:occ rel1)) (count (:occ rel2)) (count (:occ rel3)))\n   196\t            \"no $occ tuples are added\")\n   197\t        (is (= (get-in status1 [:ast-index :rows])\n   198\t               (get-in status2 [:ast-index :rows])\n   199\t               (get-in status3 [:ast-index :rows])))\n   200\t        (is (= (get-in status1 [:ast-index :occurrences])\n   201\t               (get-in status2 [:ast-index :occurrences])\n   202\t               (get-in status3 [:ast-index :occurrences])))\n   203\t        (is (= 1 (get-in status1 [:ast-index :programs])))\n   204\t        (is (= 2 (get-in status2 [:ast-index :programs])))\n   205\t        (is (= 3 (get-in status3 [:ast-index :programs]))\n   206\t            \"program counter advances while rows and occurrences remain deduplicated\")))))\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\t;; =============================================================================\n   210\t;; 5. (reset) and (vm ...) lifecycle\n   211\t;; =============================================================================\n   212\t\n   213\t(deftest reset-and-vm-selection-clear-ast-relations-fresh-eval-repopulates\n   214\t  ;; Requirement 5: (reset) and (vm ...) clear the AST relations; a fresh evaluation repopulates them.\n   215\t  (doseq [vm-type vm-types]\n   216\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n   217\t      (let [names-q '[:find ?name :in $ast :where [$ast ?id :variable ?name]]\n   218\t            [s-init _] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   219\t                                 [require-line\n   220\t                                  \"(+ 1 2)\"])\n   221\t            [s-before [before]] (evaluate s-init [(q-line names-q)])\n   222\t            [s-reset [reset-msg]] (evaluate s-before [\"(reset)\"])\n   223\t            [_ [_ after]] (evaluate s-reset [require-line (q-line names-q)])\n   224\t            [s-vm [switch-msg]] (evaluate s-before [\"(vm :ast-walker)\"])\n   225\t            [_ [_ after-vm]] (evaluate s-vm [require-line (q-line names-q)])\n   226\t            [_ [_ _ repop]] (evaluate s-reset [require-line \"(+ 1 2)\" (q-line names-q)])]\n   227\t        (is (str/includes? before \"[+]\") \"+ is present in $ast before reset\")\n   228\t        (is (= {:ast [] :occ #{}} (ast-index/relations (:ast-indexer s-reset)))\n   229\t            \"reset clears the AST relations in state\")\n   230\t        (is (str/includes? reset-msg \"reset\"))\n   231\t        (is (not (str/includes? after \"[+]\")) \"+ is absent from $ast after reset\")\n   232\t        (is (= {:ast [] :occ #{}} (ast-index/relations (:ast-indexer s-vm)))\n   233\t            \"vm selection clears the AST relations in state\")\n   234\t        (is (str/starts-with? switch-msg \"Switched to\"))\n   235\t        (is (not (str/includes? after-vm \"[+]\")) \"+ is absent from $ast after vm switch\")\n   236\t        (is (str/includes? repop \"[+]\") \"fresh evaluation repopulates the AST relations\")))))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t;; =============================================================================\n   240\t;; 6. Lost AST indexer\n   241\t;; =============================================================================\n   242\t\n   243\t(deftest lost-ast-indexer-refuses-ast-queries-while-evaluation-and-datoms-continue\n   244\t  ;; Requirement 6: A lost AST indexer (forced reader gap, as ast_index_test does)\n   245\t  ;; refuses $ast queries with index-unavailable while evaluation and $-only\n   246\t  ;; queries continue, and the round shows the AST warning line.\n   247\t  (doseq [vm-type vm-types]\n   248\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n   249\t      (let [[state _] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   250\t                                [require-line])\n   251\t            lossy (assoc-in state [:ast-indexer :observer] (lossy-observer))\n   252\t            [_ [round-text ast-res occ-res datom-res]]\n   253\t            (evaluate lossy\n   254\t                      [\"(+ 1 2)\"\n   255\t                       (q-line '[:find ?name :in $ast :where [$ast ?id :variable ?name]])\n   256\t                       (q-line '[:find ?p :in $occ :where [$occ ?r ?p ?n]])\n   257\t                       (q-line '[:find ?v . :where [?e :yin/value 1] [?e :yin/value ?v]])])]\n   258\t        (is (= (str \"3\\n\" lost-warning) round-text)\n   259\t            \"evaluation completes and the round includes the lost warning\")\n   260\t        (is (str/starts-with? ast-res \"Error: FFI call failed: $ast and $occ are unavailable\")\n   261\t            ast-res)\n   262\t        (is (str/includes? ast-res \"(:yin.repl.query/index-unavailable)\")\n   263\t            ast-res)\n   264\t        (is (str/starts-with? occ-res \"Error: FFI call failed: $ast and $occ are unavailable\")\n   265\t            occ-res)\n   266\t        (is (str/includes? occ-res \"(:yin.repl.query/index-unavailable)\")\n   267\t            occ-res)\n   268\t        (is (= (str \"1\\n\" lost-warning) datom-res)\n   269\t            \"a $-only query still succeeds and includes the round's warning\")))))\n   270\t\n   271\t\n   272\t;; =============================================================================\n   273\t;; 7. Query forms, caller input arity, and row limit\n   274\t;; =============================================================================\n   275\t\n   276\t(deftest vector-and-map-forms-arity-errors-and-result-limits\n   277\t  ;; Requirement 7: Both query vector and map forms; caller input arity errors;\n   278\t  ;; a result over the row limit.\n   279\t  (doseq [vm-type vm-types]\n   280\t    (testing (str vm-type)\n   281\t      (let [[_ [_ _ vec-res map-res arity-few arity-many]]\n   282\t            (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   283\t                      [require-line\n   284\t                       \"(+ 1 2)\"\n   285\t                       (q-line '[:find ?name :in $ast :where [$ast ?id :variable ?name]])\n   286\t                       (q-line '{:find [?name] :in [$ast] :where [[$ast ?id :variable ?name]]})\n   287\t                       (q-line '[:find ?t . :in $ast ?n :where [$ast ?id ?t ?n]])\n   288\t                       (q-line '[:find ?t . :in $ast ?n :where [$ast ?id ?t ?n]] \"1\" \"2\")])\n   289\t            [_ [_ _ limit-res]]\n   290\t            (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   291\t                      [require-line\n   292\t                       (str \"(+ \" (str/join \" \" (range 1100)) \")\")\n   293\t                       (q-line '[:find ?v :in $ast :where [$ast ?id :literal ?v]])])]\n   294\t        (is (= vec-res map-res)\n   295\t            \"vector and map query forms produce identical answers over $ast\")\n   296\t        (is (str/includes? vec-res \"[+]\")\n   297\t            \"the variable + is returned in the answer\")\n   298\t        (is (str/includes? arity-few \"(:yin.repl.query/query-failed)\")\n   299\t            arity-few)\n   300\t        (is (str/includes? arity-few \"query input arity must match :in, 1 :in inputs and an optional options map expected, got 0 arguments\")\n   301\t            arity-few)\n   302\t        (is (str/includes? arity-many \"(:yin.repl.query/query-failed)\")\n   303\t            arity-many)\n   304\t        (is (str/includes? arity-many \"query input arity must match :in, 1 :in inputs and an optional options map expected, got 2 arguments\")\n   305\t            arity-many)\n   306\t        (is (str/includes? limit-res \"(:yin.repl.query/result-limit)\")\n   307\t            limit-res)\n   308\t        (is (str/includes? limit-res (str \"over the limit of \" repl/query-row-limit))\n   309\t            limit-res)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 180 collab/1790759260000-qa-engineer-repl-ast-index-slice3.claude-opus-5-5.stdout-r2.log'","aggregated_output":"The CLJD lane (`bb test:cljd`) is still running and I don't have its result yet. I'll write the r2 report once it finishes.\n\nBoth Architect findings are fixed. I only edited `test/yin/repl/ast_query_e2e_test.cljc`.\n\n**Fix 1: shared rows, separate occurrences per root (test 3).** The substring checks are gone. The test now takes the two roots from the program stream and checks:\n- **Exact places:** reading the indexer's relations directly, the `+` node sits at exactly `#{[inner-root [2]] [outer-root [[3 0] 2]]}`.\n- **Per-root queries in the REPL:** a query with the root passed in as input returns exactly `#{[[2]]}` for the inner root and `#{[[[3 0] 2]]}` for the outer one.\n- **Counts:** there is exactly one `+` row in `$ast`, and a count query sees exactly 2 places.\n\n**Fix 2: repeated evaluation must not pass on empty relations (test 4).** After the first evaluation the test now checks that:\n- `$ast` holds exactly the rows `[:variable +]`, `[:literal 1]` and `[:literal 2]`.\n- `$occ` is not empty.\n- Every row has an occurrence, and every occurrence points to a row.\n- All occurrences sit under one root.\n\nOnly after that does it compare the full relations across the repeats.\n\n**Mutation proof.** Each mutation went into `src/cljc/yin/repl/ast_index.cljc`, then was restored. `git diff -- src` is empty.\n- **Mutation 1** paired each occurrence path with every root seen so far. All the roots and paths still show up in the output, so the old substring checks would still pass (that's reasoning; I didn't run the old test against it). The new test failed 12 times, 3 per VM: the exact place set, the inner-root query, and the count.\n- **Mutation 2** let the indexer read packets but add no rows or occurrences. The new population checks in test 4 failed on all 4 VMs. As expected, the other tests failed too.\n\n**Checks run so far:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| kondo on the file | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Focused JVM (e2e, query, ast-index) | 42 tests, 653 assertions, 0 failures |\n| Full `clj -M:test` | 2409 tests, 184936 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `bb test:cljs` | 2314 tests, 51386 assertions, 0 failures; the e2e namespace ran |\n| `bb test:cljd` | Still running |\n\nI didn't bring back the refusal test, and I didn't stage or commit anything.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
